{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Then we said to them</b> — these are the words of the builders, or the words of the scribes to those who asked them, for the phrase <i>לכום טעם</i> (to them, the reason) is explained: as it is written in the book, so we said to them who are the men building."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The phrase לכום טעם is in Aramaic, matching the Aramaic context of Ezra 4–6; translated literally as 'to them, the reason.' The overall syntax of the comment is compressed and the antecedents of 'them/they' shift rapidly between the builders, the scribes, and the questioners; translated as-is without disambiguation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:41:59.605188880Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}